The probability of getting 9 heads is given by the formula for the binomial number of heads:
\[
\frac{1}{2^{12}}} \times \binom{12}{9} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \frac{12!}{9!3!} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \frac{12 \times 11 \cdot 10}{3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times 4 \times 11 \times 10 = \frac{480}{2^{12}} = \frac{480}{1000} = 0.48
\]
The probability of getting 10 heads is:
\[
\frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \binom{12}{10} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \frac{12!}{10!2!} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \frac{12 \times 11}{2} = \frac{12 \times 11}{2 \times 2^{12}} = \frac{108}{2^{13}} = \frac{108}{2000} = 0.054
\]
The probability of getting 11 heads is:
\[
\frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \binom{12}{11} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times \frac{12!}{11!1!} = \frac{1}{2^{12}} \times 12 = \frac{12}{2^{12}} = \frac{12}{2000} = 0.006
\]
The probability of getting 12 heads is:
\[
