- \( x \) is distance along the fin
- \( k \) is the thermal conductivity of the fin material
- \( \alpha \) is the thermal conductivity to thermal diffusivity ratio
- \( A \) is the heat area of the fin
- \( \Delta T \) is the temperature difference.

Since \(k\), \(a\) and \(A\) are constant, the temperature gradient increases linearly with the temperature difference. 

