   \[
   P_{\text{pipe}} = 1000 \times 9.81 \times 5 = 4905.05 \, \text{Pa}
   \]

2. **Saturation pressure at 20°C:**
   The saturation pressure of water at 20°C is approximately 1.0135 kPa (or 1013.5 Pa). This value is readily available in tables or tables, or can be found in the reference document.

3. **Minimum inlet pressure:**
   The minimum inlet pressure required is the sum of the pressure due to the water column and the saturation pressure:
   \[
   P_{\text{min}} = P_{\text{pipe}} + P_{\text{sat}}
