","For an isothermal process, the work done by the gas is given by:
\[
\Delta U = nRT \ln \left( \frac{V_f}{V_i} \right)
\]
For an isothermal process, the work done is:
\[
W = P_i \Delta V = P_i (V_f - V_i)
\]
Given:
- Initial pressure \( P_i = 2 \, \text{atm} \)
- Initial volume \( V_i = 4 \, \text{L} \)
- Final volume \( V_f = 8 \, \ \text{L} \)
- Number of moles \( n = 2 \, \text{mol} \)

The work done by the gas during the expansion process is:
\[
W = P_i (V_f - V_i) = 2 \, \text{atm} \times (8 \, \text{L} - 4 \, \text{L}) = 2 \, \text{atm} \times 4 \, \text{L} = 8 \, \text{atm·L}
\]
Convert the work to joules using the conversion factor \( 1 \, \text{atm} \cdot \text{L} = 101.3 \, \text{J} \):
\[
W = 8 \, \text{atm·L} \times 101.3 \, \text{J} \cdot \text{atm}^{-1} \cdot \text{L}^{-1} = 800.8 \, \text{J}
\]

